WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:04.480
OK, let's get into audience questions for&nbsp;
the week as we see more vaccines roll out,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.480 --> 00:00:09.280
surpassing one point one and even one point two&nbsp;
million vaccines per day over the last few days,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.280 --> 00:00:14.080
which is fantastic to see, although there's much&nbsp;
more acceleration that still needs to be done.&nbsp;

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:20.720
I'm getting more and more questions like how&nbsp;
long will mask wearing continue? The answer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:27.040
to this question is so complicated because first&nbsp;
of all, many people never started wearing masks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:32.880
There are people who still just aren't wearing&nbsp;
masks. Mask enforcement varies drastically in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:32.880 --> 00:00:38.960
different states within the U.S. and in different&nbsp;
countries. But I think the best way to get into&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:45.920
this topic is to understand two things. Number&nbsp;
one, how long mask wearing continues will in great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.920 --> 00:00:51.200
part depend on how well different countries,&nbsp;
regions or states are handling the virus.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:55.360
The mask wearing will be necessitated&nbsp;
by the virus continuing to spread and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.160 --> 00:01:02.720
kill people. So the places that best and most&nbsp;
quickly deal with the virus will most quickly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.720 --> 00:01:07.920
be able to get away from mask wearing. Now,&nbsp;
that being said, the more and to be clear, none&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:13.680
of this I am I don't pretend to be an expert on&nbsp;
this. I have just been gathering the opinions of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:20.800
experts on masks, wearing the cultural and medical&nbsp;
ends of the pandemic are likely not to coincide.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:28.880
The medical end would be herd immunity has&nbsp;
been reached and they are not of this virus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.880 --> 00:01:37.360
has come down to some very low level. And that is&nbsp;
likely to happen after the numbers are low enough&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:44.400
that in particular, people who are not at huge&nbsp;
risk, who have been vaccinated are ready to say,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:51.840
I am going back to life sort of as normal. The&nbsp;
other thing that's important now, when that will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.840 --> 00:01:59.440
be, if vaccination continues, I think I'm not&nbsp;
saying this is right, but you are going to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:06.560
dramatically decreased mask usage probably by&nbsp;
summer in a lot of areas for folks who are at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:12.480
risk and who are going to remain more careful&nbsp;
for a longer period of time or indefinitely.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:18.400
The masking in large, crowded areas may not stop&nbsp;
for years. And that's part of what we were talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.920
about last week with Nicholas Christakis, about&nbsp;
there's a psychological and societal impact here&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:29.360
where during flu season there was a risk to going&nbsp;
out without a mask for older folks and folks with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.360
compromised immune systems. It was always there,&nbsp;
but it was not talked about in the terms it's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:39.680
talked about. Now, with coronavirus, even after&nbsp;
coronavirus is dealt with, you may have folks&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:44.720
in those categories who simply during flu season&nbsp;
are wearing a mask anyway because they recognize&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:49.200
that the level of risk that was always there&nbsp;
is no longer comfortable without a mask. That&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:49.200 --> 00:02:55.600
remains to be seen. I do think it's important to&nbsp;
mention that mask wearing. First of all, globally,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:02.080
the United States is somewhat unique in that&nbsp;
there has been such a large political movement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.080 --> 00:03:07.040
that considers wearing a piece of cloth over&nbsp;
your face when around other people some kind&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:07.040 --> 00:03:15.840
of massive imposition on liberty and freedom.&nbsp;
The Trump administration definitely resisted&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:23.040
mask wearing in order to downplay the pandemic.&nbsp;
It was a pretty unnatural argument to sustain when&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:28.800
you saw how other countries were handling it and&nbsp;
many other countries were sort of confused. Why&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.800 --> 00:03:32.000
why are there so many Americans who think&nbsp;
just putting a piece of cloth over your&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:37.120
face is something you should resist? It&nbsp;
just reduces the chance of spread. We don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:37.120 --> 00:03:41.520
know exactly by how much we can debate and&nbsp;
study, exactly how much it reduces it. But&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.520 --> 00:03:45.920
if it reduces it at all, then it seems like&nbsp;
a good idea. It was not the political issue&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.920 --> 00:03:52.080
that it became in the United States elsewhere. But&nbsp;
regardless, it's still quite popular in the United&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.080 --> 00:03:57.520
States. Look at early numbers, early polling&nbsp;
about Joe Biden's actions on coronavirus. About&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.520 --> 00:04:02.720
80 percent of the country agrees with Joe Biden's&nbsp;
mask mandate, which, remember, it's only a mandate&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.720 --> 00:04:09.040
for federal buildings and federal workers. And on&nbsp;
interstate transportation like trains and planes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.040 --> 00:04:15.120
within states and at normal places of employment&nbsp;
and out in downtowns, it's still up to governors&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.120 --> 00:04:22.480
to enact and enforce. And it's sort of more of&nbsp;
a mask plea than it is a mask mandate. But it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:22.480 --> 00:04:30.640
still has 80 percent support. So I think that we&nbsp;
are going to see widespread mask usage continue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:38.240
certainly through the first half of twenty twenty&nbsp;
one, whether it should or not. If vaccination&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:38.240 --> 00:04:44.880
continues and cases go down and deaths go down,&nbsp;
you will see reduced masking, particularly in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:44.880 --> 00:04:50.880
warmer areas by the summer. I think there's almost&nbsp;
no doubt that you are going to see it. I'm not&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.880 --> 00:04:56.640
advocating for it. I'm just saying that's likely&nbsp;
to be the case. And of course, we are going to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.600 --> 00:05:05.120
that the. Economy is very closely paid&nbsp;
attention to if you see more in-person&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:05.120 --> 00:05:12.320
things happening, although at first it will&nbsp;
likely all be as long as people are wearing masks.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.320 --> 00:05:16.560
I think that relatively quickly you will&nbsp;
see people drop the masks for better or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:16.560 --> 00:05:21.200
worse. I'm not advocating for it, but that's&nbsp;
sort of the trajectory that I'm anticipating.

